# Trivy ignores — each entry must state WHY the finding is not a real risk.
# Re-check these when the underlying package is upgraded; delete the entry once
# Trivy stops reporting it.
#
#   trivy fs --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --exit-code 1 .
#
# Verify locally before trusting: `npm ls <pkg>` must show it is NOT installed
# and `npm audit` must NOT report it. A package absent from the dependency tree
# cannot be exploited.

# undici — declared only as a devDependency of readable-stream (`^5.1.1`).
# `npm ls undici` is empty and `npm audit` does not report it, so no undici is
# shipped or reachable at runtime. Trivy still reads the root package.json
# `overrides.undici` declaration and flags it.
# CVE-2026-19534 (DoS via unrequested WebSocket subprotocol)
CVE-2026-19534

# brace-expansion — resolved to 5.0.12 (>= the 5.0.11 fix), but the lockfile
# records minimatch's dependency range `^5.0.8`, which the advisory matches.
# CVE-2026-102276 / CVE-2026-102278 (DoS via crafted brace patterns)
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278

# http-cache-semantics — pinned via overrides to 4.3.0 (the fix); Trivy reads
# the pre-override range from the lockfile.
# CVE-2026-93748 (info disclosure via max-stale)
CVE-2026-93748

# zod 3.25.76 — CVE-2023-54404 describes Zod 4 `$ZodArray` / `handleArrayResult`
# (one issue object per failing array element). Zod 3 does not contain that
# parser. Trivy still matches 3.25.76 because the advisory range starts at 0
# and lists the fix as 4.6.6, which is a Zod 4 release our packages cannot
# take (`zod` ^3.22.4). The Zod 4 copies are only the nested installs under
# `@polymarket/client` and `@polymarket/bindings`; `zod@^4.3.6` is overridden
# to ^4.6.6 and the lockfile resolves 4.6.7, which is the version Trivy treats
# as fixed. Delete this entry if `npm ls zod` shows a Zod 4 copy below 4.6.6,
# or once Trivy stops flagging 3.25.76.
# CVE-2023-54404 (DoS via unbounded array validation, Zod 4)
CVE-2023-54404